  "## The memory of the bards",
  "The Triads of the Island of Britain, Trioedd Ynys Prydain, are the memory of the old poets set out in threes: the Three Generous Men, the Three Faithful War Bands, the Three Fortunate Concealments. The oldest collection of them is in Peniarth 16, written in the thirteenth century, which keeps 46 of the 96 triads in Rachel Bromwich’s great edition.[[cite:wiki-triads]]",
  "## What else is in it",
