PAGES["peniarth-17"] = dict(people=["gruffudd-ap-cynan", "owain-gwynedd"],
 links=[("person-gruffudd-ap-cynan.html", "Gruffudd ap Cynan", "Gruffudd ap Cynan"), ("story-writers.html", "The writers who recorded early Wales", "Yr awduron a gofnododd Gymru gynnar")],
 pEn=[
  "|| Written | 13th century, second half, by one scribe",
  "|| Size | 44 pages",
  "|| Kept at | National Library of Wales (Peniarth MS 17)",
  "|| Famous for | the oldest copy of the History of Gruffudd ap Cynan",
  "## The life of a king",
  "Gruffudd ap Cynan was born in Dublin, the son of an exiled prince of Gwynedd and a princess of the Norse kings of Dublin. He fought for his kingdom for half a lifetime, was betrayed and kept in chains at Chester, escaped, and in the end ruled Gwynedd in peace until his death in 1137, the father of Owain Gwynedd. Soon after, his life was written in Latin, and it was turned into Welsh as Historia Gruffud vab Kenan: the only life of a Welsh king written in the Middle Ages.",
  "## The book",
  "Peniarth 17 is the oldest copy of the Welsh History. It is a small book of 44 pages, written in the second half of the thirteenth century by a single scribe.[[cite:nlw-pen17]] After the History come three short works of learning: on the four elements, earth, water, air and fire; on the planets; and a set of Welsh proverbs in verse.",
  "## Why it matters",
  "The History tells Gruffudd’s descent from the kings of Gwynedd and the kings of Dublin, his battles, his years of captivity, his return, and the peace and prosperity of Gwynedd in his old age, when the land was ‘bright with limewashed churches like the stars of the sky’. It is one of the great sources for the history of Wales in the age of the Norman wars, and this little book is its oldest witness.",
 ],
 pCy=[
  "|| Ysgrifennwyd | y drydedd ganrif ar ddeg, yr ail hanner, gan un copïydd",
  "|| Maint | 44 tudalen",
  "|| Cedwir yn | Llyfrgell Genedlaethol Cymru (Peniarth 17)",
  "|| Enwog am | y copi hynaf o Hanes Gruffudd ap Cynan",
  "## Bywyd brenin",
  "Ganwyd Gruffudd ap Cynan yn Nulyn, mab i dywysog alltud o Wynedd a thywysoges o deulu brenhinoedd Llychlynnaidd Dulyn. Ymladdodd am ei deyrnas am hanner oes, cafodd ei fradychu a’i gadw mewn cadwynau yng Nghaer, dihangodd, ac yn y diwedd teyrnasodd ar Wynedd mewn heddwch hyd ei farw yn 1137, yn dad i Owain Gwynedd. Yn fuan wedyn ysgrifennwyd ei fywyd yn Lladin, a throwyd ef i’r Gymraeg fel Historia Gruffud vab Kenan: yr unig fuchedd brenin o Gymro a ysgrifennwyd yn yr Oesoedd Canol.",
  "## Y llyfr",
  "Peniarth 17 yw’r copi hynaf o’r Hanes Cymraeg. Llyfr bach o 44 tudalen ydyw, a ysgrifennwyd yn ail hanner y drydedd ganrif ar ddeg gan un copïydd.[[cite:nlw-pen17]] Ar ôl yr Hanes daw tri gwaith byr o ddysg: ar y pedair elfen, daear, dŵr, awyr a thân; ar y planedau; a chyfres o ddiarhebion Cymraeg ar gân.",
  "## Pam mae’n bwysig",
  "Mae’r Hanes yn adrodd ach Gruffudd o frenhinoedd Gwynedd a brenhinoedd Dulyn, ei frwydrau, ei flynyddoedd yn garcharor, ei ddychweliad, a heddwch a ffyniant Gwynedd yn ei henaint, pan oedd y wlad ‘yn befrio gan eglwysi gwyngalchog fel sêr y ffurfafen’. Mae’n un o ffynonellau mawr hanes Cymru yn oes y rhyfeloedd â’r Normaniaid, a’r llyfr bach hwn yw ei dyst hynaf.",
 ])

